02:12:44.470 --> 02:12:47.743
I'm from London are in the UK.

02:12:47.743 --> 02:12:49.740
I've have to change my voice.

02:12:49.740 --> 02:12:51.530
They really like Royal pronunciation.

02:12:51.530 --> 02:12:53.640
Like, oi mate, how you doing? Long time.

02:12:53.640 --> 02:12:54.820
That's kinda, how I used to speak.

02:12:54.820 --> 02:12:56.010
- Do you find sometimes that you speak

02:12:56.010 --> 02:12:58.300
almost like broken English sometimes?

02:12:58.300 --> 02:12:59.290
- I've tried to stop doing that.

02:12:59.290 --> 02:13:01.943
A lot of English teachers in
Japan do the stupid voice.

02:13:01.943 --> 02:13:05.260
Like I went shopping
with my friends yesterday

02:13:05.260 --> 02:13:07.295
and they do that really, annunciate it.

02:13:07.295 --> 02:13:09.310
- Over annunciate, yeah.

02:13:09.310 --> 02:13:10.190
- Sometimes I'll talk to people

02:13:10.190 --> 02:13:12.850
and I'll just deconstruct my English live

02:13:12.850 --> 02:13:14.960
just because I'm like, I
think they'll understand

02:13:14.960 --> 02:13:15.793
if I say it this way.

02:13:15.793 --> 02:13:16.800
- Right, right.

02:13:16.800 --> 02:13:18.270
- But then I'll go on to speak to Garnt

02:13:18.270 --> 02:13:20.510
and I'll be like, "Hi Garnt.

02:13:20.510 --> 02:13:22.810
How are you today?" You know.

02:13:23.970 --> 02:13:25.267
- I lived in an environment
where for weeks at a time

02:13:25.267 --> 02:13:28.610
I was the only foreigner
around speaking English.

02:13:28.610 --> 02:13:30.030
My English level actually went down

02:13:30.030 --> 02:13:30.863
living in that environment.

02:13:30.863 --> 02:13:32.160
- Is it weird not being
able to speak English

02:13:32.160 --> 02:13:33.020
for like a month?

02:13:33.020 --> 02:13:34.010
- Yeah, it's really weird.

02:13:34.010 --> 02:13:34.920
- I've had that before as well.

02:13:34.920 --> 02:13:36.920
- Sort of bizarre issues
as a result, but like,

02:13:36.920 --> 02:13:38.970
yeah, my vocabulary level went down.

02:13:38.970 --> 02:13:41.960
I could say words like, inconsequential.

02:13:41.960 --> 02:13:43.366
Now that would come to my mind.

02:13:43.366 --> 02:13:45.781
(men laughing and speaking)

02:13:45.781 --> 02:13:46.790
- I like how that just came to your mind.

02:13:46.790 --> 02:13:48.343
I was like, what word is he gonna pick?

02:13:48.343 --> 02:13:49.930
- A word, I just went with it again,

02:13:49.930 --> 02:13:51.990
I'd be like, it just wouldn't come out.

02:13:51.990 --> 02:13:53.340
- I had that. I have that too.

02:13:53.340 --> 02:13:56.070
That like, when I first worked in a Japan,

02:13:56.070 --> 02:13:57.290
I worked in Niseko

02:13:57.290 --> 02:14:00.120
which is like a big
ski resort in Hokkaido.

02:14:00.120 --> 02:14:00.953
- Yes.

02:14:00.953 --> 02:14:01.980
- And I worked there for a month.

02:14:01.980 --> 02:14:04.760
I was like a kind of snow shoveler,

02:14:04.760 --> 02:14:06.460
general stuff around
the lobbies and stuff.

02:14:06.460 --> 02:14:08.270
But all of the people who
I worked with were just

02:14:08.270 --> 02:14:11.350
hundred percent from Hokkaido,
like all Japanese people.

02:14:11.350 --> 02:14:13.500
So I was forced to
basically speak Japanese

02:14:13.500 --> 02:14:14.740
for a month straight.

02:14:14.740 --> 02:14:15.740
And I remember,

02:14:15.740 --> 02:14:17.700
I came back to Australia and I was like,

02:14:17.700 --> 02:14:19.480
oh, it's only been a month, right?

02:14:19.480 --> 02:14:21.480
Of course, English is my first language.

02:14:21.480 --> 02:14:22.313
Of course, I'm not gonna forget it.

02:14:22.313 --> 02:14:23.270
But then I came back to Australia.

02:14:23.270 --> 02:14:26.221
I was like, shit what was that word again?

02:14:26.221 --> 02:14:28.530
I would actually forget something.

02:14:28.530 --> 02:14:29.363
- Inconsequential.

02:14:29.363 --> 02:14:30.413
- Yeah!
(men laughing)

02:14:30.413 --> 02:14:32.210
- Inconse-something rather, fuck.

02:14:32.210 --> 02:14:34.050
I don't know how to say it. Hard.

02:14:34.050 --> 02:14:35.800
You know? It was just really difficult.

02:14:35.800 --> 02:14:38.430
- But like, in terms of like
dumbing down your language

02:14:38.430 --> 02:14:40.470
when speaking to like, you
know, Japanese speakers,

02:14:40.470 --> 02:14:41.951
I feel like anyone

02:14:41.951 --> 02:14:44.840
who has come from like a bilingual parents

02:14:44.840 --> 02:14:47.010
or like is bilingual
and has had like Asian,

02:14:47.010 --> 02:14:50.530
or parents who don't speak
your native language as well,

02:14:50.530 --> 02:14:52.420
it's something I've just grown up with.

02:14:52.420 --> 02:14:55.550
Cause whenever I, whenever
I speak to my parents,

02:14:55.550 --> 02:14:56.790
like mostly like for example,

02:14:56.790 --> 02:14:58.500
when I speak to my mom,
I mostly speak in Thai.

02:14:58.500 --> 02:15:00.540
But when I have to express
something in English,

02:15:00.540 --> 02:15:03.500
I like very much have to
dumb down my language.

02:15:03.500 --> 02:15:05.600
Very careful about how I word things.

02:15:05.600 --> 02:15:07.100
Cause especially like learning a language,

02:15:07.100 --> 02:15:09.150
you know how their grammar structure is.

02:15:09.150 --> 02:15:12.190
So, you know, like sometimes
you hear a Japanese people,

02:15:12.190 --> 02:15:14.060
like Japanese person speak,
try to speak English.

02:15:14.060 --> 02:15:17.030
And like, you understand
what their like mentality is

02:15:17.030 --> 02:15:18.810
or what their like, train of thought is

02:15:18.810 --> 02:15:21.200
when they're trying to
construct a sentence.

02:15:21.200 --> 02:15:23.170
Kind of like, what you kind of learn to do

02:15:23.170 --> 02:15:24.290
is kind of mirror the way

02:15:24.290 --> 02:15:26.810
that they would construct a sentence,

02:15:26.810 --> 02:15:28.430
so that they would more
easily understand it.

02:15:28.430 --> 02:15:30.030
- Yeah. Especially what
I find myself doing.

02:15:30.030 --> 02:15:30.863
- Yeah.
- But also,

02:15:30.863 --> 02:15:31.900
oh, dude. I forget.

02:15:31.900 --> 02:15:34.910
Like, so I'll think of a word in Welsh.

02:15:34.910 --> 02:15:36.043
And I'll remember the
Japanese word for it.

02:15:36.043 --> 02:15:38.040
And I'm like, what the fuck is it?

02:15:38.040 --> 02:15:39.130
Which one is it? And then vice versa.

02:15:39.130 --> 02:15:40.280
I'll be speaking Japanese.

02:15:40.280 --> 02:15:41.740
And I'll be like,

02:15:41.740 --> 02:15:43.879
why is the Walsh word
keep popping up in my head

02:15:43.879 --> 02:15:45.100
when I'm trying to
think of the right word?

02:15:45.100 --> 02:15:45.933
It's a mess

02:15:45.933 --> 02:15:46.950
cause I obviously don't
use those languages

02:15:46.950 --> 02:15:48.110
as much as I use English.

02:15:48.110 --> 02:15:49.160
So in my head they're slowly

02:15:49.160 --> 02:15:51.980
like, amalgamating
together and it's awful.

02:15:51.980 --> 02:15:53.170
- I guess you're kinda
getting to the point

02:15:53.170 --> 02:15:54.830
and you as well Connor, you kind of,

02:15:54.830 --> 02:15:55.850
you guys came to the point where

02:15:55.850 --> 02:15:57.820
you're learning a third language, right?

02:15:57.820 --> 02:15:58.720
- I mean, yeah.

02:15:58.720 --> 02:16:00.201
I mean, I try and use it.

02:16:00.201 --> 02:16:01.210
- Japanese for you, is technically

02:16:01.210 --> 02:16:02.870
like a third language
you're trying to learn.

02:16:02.870 --> 02:16:04.470
- Right?
- I try and use it

02:16:04.470 --> 02:16:05.360
as much as possible.

02:16:05.360 --> 02:16:08.896
I mean, I'm doing like on
the, my new second channel.

02:16:08.896 --> 02:16:10.259
- Whoa!
- Wow!

02:16:10.259 --> 02:16:11.092
- He's plugging his second channel.

02:16:11.092 --> 02:16:12.480
- Wow Wow. Yeah, plug!

02:16:12.480 --> 02:16:15.330
I'm doing a series where
I'm, I guess, playing games

02:16:15.330 --> 02:16:18.970
with Japanese people and using
what broken Japanese I have.

02:16:18.970 --> 02:16:20.013
And sometimes I'm like about to say a word

02:16:20.013 --> 02:16:22.620
and I'm like, nope, that's the Welsh word.

02:16:22.620 --> 02:16:23.693
But if you haven't watched that,

02:16:23.693 --> 02:16:24.526
you should come watch it.

02:16:24.526 --> 02:16:25.359
If you wanna see my terrible,

02:16:25.359 --> 02:16:27.010
my terrible Japanese in action.

02:16:27.010 --> 02:16:28.000
But I do find that

02:16:28.000 --> 02:16:29.850
that has been the best
practice had though.

02:16:29.850 --> 02:16:30.683
Which is just talking.

02:16:30.683 --> 02:16:31.516
_ Oh yeah.
_ Yeah.

02:16:31.516 --> 02:16:34.050
- Because unfortunately I'm
at a very privileged situation

02:16:34.050 --> 02:16:36.560
where I don't need to
talk to Japanese people.

02:16:36.560 --> 02:16:37.840
Which, I mean, you know.

02:16:37.840 --> 02:16:39.300
