they have real tummul.

02:19:02.435 --> 02:19:03.268
(man speaking in Japanese)

02:19:03.268 --> 02:19:05.060
Yeah. So when you game online with people,

02:19:05.060 --> 02:19:06.740
they're not the real friends.

02:19:06.740 --> 02:19:07.573
- Right.

02:19:07.573 --> 02:19:08.406
- Then sometimes if
you're busy, you're like,

02:19:08.406 --> 02:19:09.901
oh, I'm playing with real tummel.

02:19:09.901 --> 02:19:10.734
- Oh!

02:19:10.734 --> 02:19:11.804
- Actual, real friend.

02:19:11.804 --> 02:19:14.860
- Diatomo is like the
equivalent of like, IRL friends.

02:19:14.860 --> 02:19:18.070
- Yeah, which is funny cause
it's like, you're not real.

02:19:18.070 --> 02:19:18.903
- That's interesting.

02:19:18.903 --> 02:19:19.980
- You're my gaming friend.

02:19:19.980 --> 02:19:20.996
You're not my real friend.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

02:19:20.996 --> 02:19:22.670
I've been learning a
lot through doing that.

02:19:22.670 --> 02:19:24.810
- Yeah. There's a lot of like Japanese,

02:19:24.810 --> 02:19:26.070
I guess like internet slang,

02:19:26.070 --> 02:19:27.920
you'll learn from
playing Japanese players.

02:19:27.920 --> 02:19:29.700
- Yeah, luckily I've
been playing with one guy

02:19:29.700 --> 02:19:31.160
and he's been figuring out

02:19:31.160 --> 02:19:32.650
how to like dumb things down for me.

02:19:32.650 --> 02:19:33.483
- Right, right.
- Which is good,

02:19:33.483 --> 02:19:34.316
because sometimes he talks too fast.

02:19:34.316 --> 02:19:36.896
- If he was like throwing
out, like 2Chan lingo.

02:19:36.896 --> 02:19:40.380
- I feel like they never use like any,

02:19:40.380 --> 02:19:42.360
they always use like plain
form and stuff like that.

02:19:42.360 --> 02:19:43.193
And throw that at me.

02:19:43.193 --> 02:19:45.660
Fucking gee, this is
not one of my classes.

02:19:45.660 --> 02:19:46.860
What's all this nonsense?

02:19:46.860 --> 02:19:48.240
- Where is the (man speaking Japanese)?

02:19:49.080 --> 02:19:50.900
- He hasn't said watashiwa once!

02:19:50.900 --> 02:19:52.523
What's going on here?

02:19:55.410 --> 02:19:58.290
I feel like watashiwa is the
biggest fucking lie you learn.

02:19:58.290 --> 02:19:59.433
- Yeah.
- Duolingo.

02:19:59.433 --> 02:20:00.610
(man speaking Japanese)

02:20:00.610 --> 02:20:01.460
Yeah.
- Nobody says that.

02:20:01.460 --> 02:20:02.760
- On Duolingo,

02:20:02.760 --> 02:20:04.890
it constantly throws
watashi nonstop at you.

02:20:04.890 --> 02:20:06.670
- It's the first thing you learn.

02:20:06.670 --> 02:20:07.503
- Right!

02:20:07.503 --> 02:20:09.480
- Every Japanese textbook,
in every classroom.

02:20:09.480 --> 02:20:10.430
- And then you talk to them,

02:20:10.430 --> 02:20:11.700
and you're like, so
that was a fucking lie.

02:20:11.700 --> 02:20:14.590
- I have to say now, to everyone
who messages me every day

02:20:14.590 --> 02:20:16.480
saying they've learned
Japanese from Duolingo.

02:20:16.480 --> 02:20:17.800
It doesn't prepare you for Japanese.

02:20:17.800 --> 02:20:19.360
Duolingo is fun. It's quite fun.

02:20:19.360 --> 02:20:20.717
But like, yeah, it won't prepare you

02:20:20.717 --> 02:20:21.984
for on the ground Japanese.

02:20:21.984 --> 02:20:23.873
- For a little mini game, it is.

02:20:23.873 --> 02:20:24.706
(man laughing)

02:20:24.706 --> 02:20:25.570
- It helps with vocab.

02:20:25.570 --> 02:20:26.910
But that's honestly, as far as it goes.

02:20:26.910 --> 02:20:28.930
But even then I, cause sometimes Duolingo

02:20:28.930 --> 02:20:31.210
